{"name":"Down Feathers","hex":"#fff9e7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"down feathers","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of down feather"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/down_feathers"}],"entries":[{"title":"Down feather","blocks":[{"text":"The down of birds is a layer of fine feathers found under the tougher exterior feathers. Very young birds are clad only in down. Powder down is a specialized type of down found only in a few groups of birds. Down is a fine thermal insulator and padding, used in goods such as jackets, bedding, pillows and sleeping bags. The discovery of feathers trapped in ancient amber suggests that some species of non-avian dinosaur likely possessed down-like feathers."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Donsvlokje.jpg/330px-Donsvlokje.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Down_feather"},{"title":"Feather","blocks":[{"text":"Feathers are epidermal growths that form a distinctive outer covering, or plumage, on both avian (bird) and some non-avian dinosaurs and other archosaurs. They are the most complex integumentary structures found in vertebrates and an example of a complex evolutionary novelty. They are among the characteristics that distinguish the extant birds from other living groups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Types_de_plumes._-_Larousse_pour_tous%2C_-1907-1910-.jpg/330px-Types_de_plumes._-_Larousse_pour_tous%2C_-1907-1910-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feather"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Chick.jpg/500px-Chick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Chick.jpg/1280px-Chick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Chick.jpg/500px-Chick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Like many precocial hatchlings, domestic chickens are already covered with a coat of downy feathers when they hatch.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChick.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Bird_Imprint_on_Window_0069.jpg/500px-Bird_Imprint_on_Window_0069.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Bird_Imprint_on_Window_0069.jpg/500px-Bird_Imprint_on_Window_0069.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"\"Feather dust\" left on a window after a birdstrike","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABird_Imprint_on_Window_0069.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Melopsittacus_undulatus_-_male_pet_preening.jpg/500px-Melopsittacus_undulatus_-_male_pet_preening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Melopsittacus_undulatus_-_male_pet_preening.jpg/500px-Melopsittacus_undulatus_-_male_pet_preening.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Body down feathers, like these exposed on this adult male budgerigar's back, lie underneath the contour feathers and help to insulate birds against heat loss.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMelopsittacus_undulatus_-_male_pet_preening.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Eider.a.duvet4.jpg/500px-Eider.a.duvet4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Eider.a.duvet4.jpg/500px-Eider.a.duvet4.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.o